-- P5-art-43-annex-vi: Article 43 (conformity assessment) and Annex VI (conformity assessment procedure based on internal control).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026 (a plain-text rendering with no legal effect);
-- src:N is its line N, src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:N is the as-enacted text. Annex VII (the procedure with a notified body) is another part's;
-- the procedures are named here, not restated. Group: General (Art 113 second paragraph, assumed: keel fork F-113-groups).
-- Article 43(3) was REPLACED by the Omnibus: both texts are encoded, each in its own function, with a dispatcher on the version in force.
-- The as-enacted text applied only until 26 July 2026 and the group applies only from 2 August 2026, so a dispatcher's as-enacted branch can
-- never be reached through the gate (PLAN.md section 5): each as-enacted function is tested directly.
-- Articles 43(5) and 43(6) are delegated-act powers over the Annexes (machinery, inert: NOTES.md).

§ `Article 43: the procedures, and who acts as a notified body`

-- The procedures the text gives. A constructor is the text's own answer; NOTHING is "not covered".
DECLARE `Art 43 procedure` IS ONE OF
    `Art 43 procedure of Annex VI (internal control)`
    `Art 43 procedure of Annex VII (quality management system and technical documentation, with a notified body)`
    `Art 43(1) option between the procedure of Annex VI and the procedure of Annex VII`
    `Art 43(1) procedure of Annex VII for the restricted part of the harmonised standard only`
    `Art 43(3) procedure required by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`

DECLARE `Art 43(1) body` IS ONE OF
    `Art 43(1) any notified body chosen by the provider`
    `Art 43(1) the market surveillance authority referred to in Article 74(8) or (9)`

§§ `Article 43(1): high-risk AI systems listed in point 1 of Annex III`

-- First and second subparagraphs read together. First subparagraph: where the provider has applied harmonised standards or, where applicable,
-- common specifications, "the provider shall opt for one of" the Annex VI or the Annex VII procedure. Second subparagraph: the provider "shall
-- follow" Annex VII where (a), (b), (c) or (d). The points are alternatives (the text separates them with semicolons and no "and"): fork F-43-1.
-- Point (b) is read as the case where a harmonised standard exists and the provider has not applied it or has applied only part of it
-- (fork F-43-1b): the question is put to the provider in those words. "listed in point 1 of Annex III" is Annex III's (another part): a plain input.
-- src:675 | 1. For high-risk AI systems listed in point 1 of Annex III, where, in demonstrating the compliance of a high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2, the provider has applied harmonised standards referred to in Article 40, or, where applicable, common specifications referred to in Article 41, the provider shall opt for one of the following conformity assessment procedures based on:
-- src:676 | (a) the internal control referred to in Annex VI; or
-- src:677 | (b) the assessment of the quality management system and the assessment of the technical documentation, with the involvement of a notified body, referred to in Annex VII.
-- src:678 | In demonstrating the compliance of a high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2, the provider shall follow the conformity assessment procedure set out in Annex VII where:
-- src:679 | (a) harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 do not exist, and common specifications referred to in Article 41 are not available;
-- src:680 | (b) the provider has not applied, or has applied only part of, the harmonised standard;
-- src:681 | (c) the common specifications referred to in point (a) exist, but the provider has not applied them;
-- src:682 | (d) one or more of the harmonised standards referred to in point (a) has been published with a restriction, and only on the part of the standard that was restricted.
@ref Art 43(1), first and second subparagraphs (src:675-682)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` IS A NUMBER
      `the provider has applied harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 or, where applicable, common specifications referred to in Article 41` IS A BOOLEAN
      `harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 do not exist, and common specifications referred to in Article 41 are not available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has not applied, or has applied only part of, the harmonised standard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the common specifications referred to in point (a) exist, but the provider has not applied them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more of the harmonised standards referred to in point (a) has been published with a restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 43 procedure`
`Art 43(1) the conformity assessment procedure the provider is to follow` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 43 1)
    THEN NOTHING  -- S14-kind (not a yes or no answer): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF NOT (`the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` EQUALS 1)
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For high-risk AI systems listed in point 1 of Annex III" (a scope limit with no "only": ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))
              ELSE IF       `harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 do not exist, and common specifications referred to in Article 41 are not available`
                         OR `the provider has not applied, or has applied only part of, the harmonised standard`
                         OR `the common specifications referred to in point (a) exist, but the provider has not applied them`
                   THEN JUST `Art 43 procedure of Annex VII (quality management system and technical documentation, with a notified body)`
                   ELSE IF `one or more of the harmonised standards referred to in point (a) has been published with a restriction`
                        THEN JUST `Art 43(1) procedure of Annex VII for the restricted part of the harmonised standard only`
                        ELSE IF `the provider has applied harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 or, where applicable, common specifications referred to in Article 41`
                             THEN JUST `Art 43(1) option between the procedure of Annex VI and the procedure of Annex VII`
                             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provider has applied neither, and none of points (a) to (d) is stated to hold

-- Third subparagraph: the body that carries out the Annex VII procedure. "the provider may choose any of the notified bodies. However, where ...
-- the market surveillance authority ... shall act as a notified body." In the excepted case the choice is taken away: the answer names the authority.
-- src:683 | For the purposes of the conformity assessment procedure referred to in Annex VII, the provider may choose any of the notified bodies. However, where the high-risk AI system is intended to be put into service by law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities or by Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies, the market surveillance authority referred to in Article 74(8) or (9), as applicable, shall act as a notified body.
@ref Art 43(1), third subparagraph (src:683)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII is carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system is intended to be put into service by law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities or by Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 43(1) body`
`Art 43(1) the body that carries out the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 43 1)
    THEN NOTHING  -- S14-kind (not a yes or no answer): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF NOT `the conformity assessment procedure of Annex VII is carried out`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of the conformity assessment procedure referred to in Annex VII"
              ELSE IF `the high-risk AI system is intended to be put into service by law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities or by Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies`
                   THEN JUST `Art 43(1) the market surveillance authority referred to in Article 74(8) or (9)`
                   ELSE JUST `Art 43(1) any notified body chosen by the provider`

§§ `Article 43(2): high-risk AI systems referred to in points 2 to 8 of Annex III`

-- src:684 | 2. For high-risk AI systems referred to in points 2 to 8 of Annex III, providers shall follow the conformity assessment procedure based on internal control as referred to in Annex VI, which does not provide for the involvement of a notified body.
@ref Art 43(2) (src:684)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 43 procedure`
`Art 43(2) the conformity assessment procedure the provider is to follow` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 43 2)
    THEN NOTHING  -- S14-kind (not a yes or no answer): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF       `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` AT LEAST 2
                   AND `the point of Annex III under which the high-risk AI system is listed` AT MOST 8
              THEN JUST `Art 43 procedure of Annex VI (internal control)`
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "high-risk AI systems referred to in points 2 to 8 of Annex III"

§§ `Article 43(3): high-risk AI systems covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I (REPLACED by the Omnibus)`

-- First subparagraph, first sentence. Wording only: the text as enacted says "the provider shall follow ... as required under those legal acts", the text
-- as amended says "the provider of the system shall follow ... as required in accordance with the relevant Union harmonisation legislation": the same
-- answer, shown by a test on each function (NOTES.md, Versions).
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1214 | 3. For high-risk AI systems covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, the provider shall follow the relevant conformity assessment procedure as required under those legal acts.
