             ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the date "28 January 2028" has not yet passed, so the duty is not yet breached

§§ `Article 43(3) third subparagraph: the product manufacturer's option (the text as enacted and the text as amended, and the two sentences the Omnibus added)`

-- First sentence. The two texts differ in what the manufacturer must have applied to qualify for the legislation's option: as enacted "all harmonised standards covering all
-- the relevant requirements", as amended "harmonised standards to ensure compliance with all the relevant requirements" (no "all" before "harmonised standards"): the
-- dispatcher takes both facts. Gates: "Where ... provides" fails: JUST FALSE ("where": ruling (b), a "may" gated by "where": split site (ii), fork F-43-3-opt);
-- "provided that" fails: NOTHING (the grant ruling, same fork); "only if" fails: JUST FALSE (the text closes the gate itself).
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1216 | Where a legal act listed in Section A of Annex I enables the product manufacturer to opt out from a third-party conformity assessment, provided that that manufacturer has applied all harmonised standards covering all the relevant requirements, that manufacturer may use that option only if it has also applied harmonised standards or, where applicable, common specifications referred to in Article 41, covering all requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter.
@ref Art 43(3) third subparagraph, as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1216)
GIVEN `a legal act listed in Section A of Annex I enables the product manufacturer to opt out from a third-party conformity assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manufacturer has applied all harmonised standards covering all the relevant requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manufacturer has also applied harmonised standards or, where applicable, common specifications referred to in Article 41, covering all requirements set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 43(3) third subparagraph as enacted the product manufacturer may use the option not to have a third-party conformity assessment` MEANS
    IF NOT `a legal act listed in Section A of Annex I enables the product manufacturer to opt out from a third-party conformity assessment`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a legal act listed in Section A of Annex I enables the product manufacturer to opt out" (a "where" gate on a "may": reading (b), fork F-43-3-opt)
    ELSE IF NOT `the manufacturer has applied all harmonised standards covering all the relevant requirements`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "provided that that manufacturer has applied all harmonised standards covering all the relevant requirements" (a grant: fork F-43-3-opt)
         ELSE IF `the manufacturer has also applied harmonised standards or, where applicable, common specifications referred to in Article 41, covering all requirements set out in Section 2`
              THEN JUST TRUE  -- VERSION as enacted
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that manufacturer may use that option only if it has also applied harmonised standards or, where applicable, common specifications"

