§§ `Article 43(4): a substantial modification`

-- First subparagraph. "that have already been subject to a conformity assessment procedure" is the subject (a scope limit with no "only": NOTHING outside it); "in the event of a
-- substantial modification" is a condition (an "if" variant on a duty: JUST FALSE where it fails). "substantial modification" is Art 3(23): the caller computes it.
-- src:691 | 4. High-risk AI systems that have already been subject to a conformity assessment procedure shall undergo a new conformity assessment procedure in the event of a substantial modification, regardless of whether the modified system is intended to be further distributed or continues to be used by the current deployer.
@ref Art 43(4) first subparagraph (src:691)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI system has already been subject to a conformity assessment procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is a substantial modification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 43(4) the high-risk AI system must undergo a new conformity assessment procedure` MEANS
    IF (`Art 40 to 49 Art 2(2) cuts the provision off from the high-risk AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 43 4)
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- S14-kind (a list closed by "only"): Article 2(2), "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113's general date has not come, or Art 111(2) saves the system
         ELSE IF NOT `the high-risk AI system has already been subject to a conformity assessment procedure`
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "High-risk AI systems that have already been subject to a conformity assessment procedure" (a scope limit with no "only")
              ELSE IF `the change is a substantial modification`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the event of a substantial modification" (reading (a): a failed "if" within the provision)

-- Second subparagraph: "shall not constitute a substantial modification" (a flat negative): the function says the change is excluded.
-- src:692 | For high-risk AI systems that continue to learn after being placed on the market or put into service, changes to the high-risk AI system and its performance that have been pre-determined by the provider at the moment of the initial conformity assessment and are part of the information contained in the technical documentation referred to in point 2(f) of Annex IV, shall not constitute a substantial modification.
@ref Art 43(4) second subparagraph (src:692)
GIVEN `the high-risk AI system continues to learn after being placed on the market or put into service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the changes to the high-risk AI system and its performance have been pre-determined by the provider at the moment of the initial conformity assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the changes are part of the information contained in the technical documentation referred to in point 2(f) of Annex IV` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 43(4) the changes do not constitute a substantial modification` MEANS
    IF       `the high-risk AI system continues to learn after being placed on the market or put into service`
         AND `the changes to the high-risk AI system and its performance have been pre-determined by the provider at the moment of the initial conformity assessment`
         AND `the changes are part of the information contained in the technical documentation referred to in point 2(f) of Annex IV`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says: "shall not constitute a substantial modification"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exclusion reaches only changes of a learning system that were pre-determined and documented; for any other change Art 3(23) decides

§§ `Article 43(5) and (6): inert`

-- Article 43(5) and (6): the Commission's power to adopt delegated acts amending Annexes VI and VII and paragraphs 1 and 2: a rule-making power (machinery, reason 2);
-- the amendment, if made, is made by a delegated act that is not among the sources. No rule here (NOTES.md, Coverage).

§§ `Article 43: the regulative rules`

DECLARE `Art 43 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 43(1) opt for the procedure of Annex VI or the procedure of Annex VII`
    `Art 43(1) follow the procedure of Annex VII`
    `Art 43(1) choose a notified body`
    `Art 43(2) follow the procedure of Annex VI`
    `Art 43(3) follow the procedure required by the Union harmonisation legislation`
    `Art 43(3) use the option not to have a third-party conformity assessment`
    `Art 43(3) assess the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2`
    `Art 43(3) apply for designation in accordance with Section 4`
    `Art 43(4) undergo a new conformity assessment procedure`

DECLARE `Art 43 authority` IS ONE OF
    `Art 43 the market surveillance authority referred to in Article 74(8) or (9)`

DECLARE `Art 43 authority act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 43(1) act as a notified body`

-- Each provider rule names a party and an act. None states a time limit or a consequence, so none can reach BREACH (NOTES.md: Rules with no breach path);
-- the one rule with a date, the notified body's application for designation (28 January 2028), has a breach path and a trace that reaches it.
-- The gate is the same as the decision function's: nothing is owed (FULFILLED) where the group does not apply or Art 111(2) saves the system.
@ref Art 43(1), first subparagraph
